  "description": "XASDON crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C142 H128 Dy4 N10 O38 Zn6 2+,2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1B (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2B (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3B (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.127-3.813 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.57-123.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn6Dy4(OH)2(L1)10(MeOH)2(H2O)4]Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
